{
  "mn139:0.1": "Middle Discourses 139 ",
  "mn139:0.2": "The Analysis of No Strife ",
  "mn139:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn139:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn139:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn139:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn139:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn139:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn139:2.1": "“Mendicants, I shall teach you the analysis of no strife. ",
  "mn139:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn139:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn139:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn139:3.1": "“Don’t indulge in sensual pleasure, which is low, crude, ordinary, ignoble, and pointless. And don’t indulge in self-mortification, which is painful, ignoble, and pointless. ",
  "mn139:3.2": "Avoiding these two extremes, the Realized One understood the middle way of practice, which gives vision and knowledge, and leads to peace, direct knowledge, awakening, and extinguishment. ",
  "mn139:3.3": "Know what it means to flatter and to rebuke. ",
  "mn139:3.4": "Knowing these, avoid them, and just teach Dhamma. ",
  "mn139:3.5": "Know how to evaluate different kinds of pleasure. ",
  "mn139:3.6": "Knowing this, pursue inner pleasure. ",
  "mn139:3.7": "Don’t talk behind people’s backs, and don’t speak sharply in their presence. ",
  "mn139:3.8": "Don’t speak hurriedly. ",
  "mn139:3.9": "Don’t insist on popular defin